<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<UserControl
    x:Class="Winhance.UI.Features.Common.Controls.FeatureOutcomeBanner"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:local="using:Winhance.UI.Features.Common.Controls">

    <!--
    Reports, on a feature's overview card, that Winhance could not determine the state of some settings
    inside it. Sits directly below the card, the same Border + QuietInfoBar pattern the settings cards
    already use, so the two levels of the app explain a problem the same way.

    This REPLACED per-outcome info-badge pills. A detection outcome is a fault, not a badge: badges say
    where a value sits relative to our advice, which is optional detail and reasonably hidden behind
    View > InfoBadges. Hiding "1 setting is saved in the wrong format" behind that same toggle was
    backwards - so this is deliberately NOT gated by it. The Recommended / Default pills on the card
    above still are, because those genuinely are optional detail.

    ONE banner, never three. An InfoBar carries a single Severity, so three stacked bars would also mean
    three colours, reading as three separate incidents rather than one section worth a look. The severity
    is the WORST outcome present - red "couldn't read" outranks amber "wrong format" outranks blue
    "not recognized" - which is the same ladder the settings cards use, so a colour means the same thing
    everywhere. The message then names every kind that is actually present, so nothing is hidden by the
    one that won.
    -->
    <Border Visibility="{x:Bind BannerVisibility, Mode=OneWay}" Margin="0,-4,0,0">
        <local:QuietInfoBar
            IsOpen="{x:Bind IsBannerOpen, Mode=OneWay}"
            Severity="{x:Bind BannerSeverity, Mode=OneWay}"
            Message="{x:Bind BannerMessage, Mode=OneWay}"
            IconSource="{x:Bind BannerIconSource, Mode=OneWay}"
            IsClosable="False"
            IsTabStop="True"
            UseSystemFocusVisuals="True"
            CornerRadius="4"/>
    </Border>
</UserControl>
